<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch14-parametric-curves-polar-coordinates-and-conics">
  <title>Parametric Curves, Polar Coordinates, and Conics</title>
  <shorttitle>Parametric and Polar Curves</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>A plane curve need not be the graph of a single function <m>y=f(x)</m>. Parametric equations describe both coordinates using one parameter, and polar coordinates describe position using a radius and angle. This chapter develops calculus in these coordinates, studies conic sections and planetary motion, and introduces complex numbers in polar form.</p></introduction>

